Ladybird preserves the author’s line-height on selects without
native appearance, including inherited and animated line-height.
The computed appearance controls the native line-height reset, and
changes to appearance rebuild the affected font metrics.

Blink’s LayoutTheme::AdjustStyle() returns before native adjustments
when the effective appearance is none. Its AdjustMenuListStyle()
resets line-height for a native menu list. Chrome gives the reduced
page’s unthemed selects a 26px line-height and a 68px border-box height,
matching the neighboring inputs. Its native select retains normal.

WebKit’s RenderTheme::adjustStyle() returns when the style has no used
appearance. Its RenderThemeMac::adjustMenuListButtonStyle() resets
line-height within the native menu-list styling path. In Gecko, the
StyleAdjuster::adjust_for_appearance() method resets line-height only
for an HTML select whose effective appearance is Menulist. All three
leave the author’s value intact for a select with “appearance: none”.
